  "title": "Work & school",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**যাওয়া** 'go' follows the same person pattern: **আমি যাই**, **তুমি যাও**, **আপনি যান**, **সে যায়**. (You met **যান** as a polite command in Unit 7 — the present and the command look the same.)\n\n**আসা** 'come': **আমি আসি**, **সে আসে**.\n\nDestinations take the locative **-এ**: **অফিসে যাই** 'I go to the office', **স্কুলে যায়** 'goes to school'. With বাসা it's **বাসায়**.\n\n**Culture:** in Bangladesh the work/school week usually runs Sunday to Thursday; Friday (and often Saturday) is the weekend.",
